# This library logs people in. Anything it produces while being worked on -
# a cached session, a failed login's hop-by-hop trace - names a real person
# and is a live credential besides. Those normally land in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME,
# but a run started from here could drop one in the working directory, so the
# rule is blunt: no data file, anywhere in the tree, ever gets committed.
*.json
*.txt
*.har
*-session*
*-login-report*

# ...except what the tests are built on, which is invented.
!tests/**

# Python
__pycache__/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
